<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The station list (SPEC §7.2), lying down.

    Same screen, same views, same reading — what changes is what the rows are
    measured against. Stacked as in portrait, the header costs the same dp
    whichever way the phone is held: a title, a freshness line, a field and a
    toggle. On a Fairphone 3 turned sideways the window stops at 397 px once
    Gboard is open, and that header takes all of it — the list came out a row
    and a half tall, and the "nearest station first" button, which hangs from
    the bottom edge the keyboard has just pushed up, ended over the field it
    had nothing to do with, half covering the cross that clears it.

    So the header and the rows share the width instead of the height, and the
    whole header — the title, the data's age, the three ways out, the field and
    the toggle — lives in the column on the start side. Nothing spans both:
    the rows start at the top of the screen and end at the bottom of it, and
    the button hangs from a column as tall as the window.

    Half and not some finer split for the reason written in
    `layout-land/fragment_welcome.xml`: half a sideways Fairphone 3 is 411 dp,
    exactly the width the portrait screen gives the same rows, so a station's
    name and its counts wrap and read as they always have. **The half is a
    percentage anchored to the start edge, and no bias**: a bias is measured
    from the left whichever way the language runs, and this screen is read
    right to left in Arabic. Each column carries one anchor and its own half,
    so the two mirror together with the language. A chain would mirror too, but
    a chain needs both its links to be children of this layout, and the header
    is no longer one child.

    **The header column scrolls, and that is the whole of what a text size can
    do to it.** The first sideways arrangement seated the title and the data's
    age inside the row of icons, whose height is 48 dp of touch target: at a
    text size of ×2.0 the freshness no longer fitted, and being centred in that
    row it lost what did not fit off the top of the screen — "Aktualisiert vor
    59 Sekunden" measured `[457,0][670,320]`, its first word cut above the edge.
    SPEC §7 has the height give way, never the letters, and the comment beside
    `mode_toggle` in `fragment_map.xml` records the same defect being fixed the
    same way on the map.

    Here nothing is centred in a fixed height any more. The row of the title is
    an ordinary row that wraps its tallest child, so the data's age keeps the
    title's line where it fits on it — which is what buys the field the 53 px
    it needs at the ordinary text sizes — and takes a second and a third line
    when it does not, the row growing under it. What the growing pushes past
    the bottom of a window a keyboard has shortened is scrolled to, and the
    field, being the focused view, is scrolled back into sight by the scroll
    view itself when the keyboard opens. At ×2.0 the header is simply taller
    than a sideways window: 36 dp of inset, a 64 dp row, a 72 dp field. There
    is no arrangement that fits it, and the choice is between letters lost and
    a column one scrolls.
-->
<androidx.constraintlayout.widget.ConstraintLayout
    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:fitsSystemWindows="true">

    <!-- The header's half of the width, and as much height as it asks for. -->
    <androidx.core.widget.NestedScrollView
        android:layout_width="0dp"
        android:layout_height="0dp"
        app:layout_constraintBottom_toBottomOf="parent"
        app:layout_constraintStart_toStartOf="parent"
        app:layout_constraintTop_toTopOf="parent"
        app:layout_constraintWidth_default="percent"
        app:layout_constraintWidth_percent="0.5">

        <LinearLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:orientation="vertical"
            android:paddingTop="@dimen/space_s"
            android:paddingBottom="@dimen/space_m">

            <!-- The title, the data's age and the three ways out on one row,
                 which portrait gives three. The row wraps its tallest child:
                 the icons are 48 dp of touch target and the two texts are
                 written in `sp`, so at the ordinary sizes the row is the
                 icons' and at ×2.0 it is the freshness's. Nothing is centred
                 in a height it cannot have, which is the defect this file was
                 rewritten for.

                 The three keep the order they have in portrait — settings
                 outermost, the map innermost — and a row lays its children out
                 from the start, so the order mirrors with the language on its
                 own. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:paddingStart="@dimen/space_l"
                android:paddingEnd="@dimen/space_s">

                <!-- No wider than its own words: what follows it on this row is
                     the freshness, and a title box running under the text
                     beside it is only harmless while the text is left-aligned.
                     In Arabic it is right-aligned. -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/title"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:text="@string/stations_title"
                    android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.RoueLibre.Title" />

                <!-- The data's age, required by SPEC §4.1. It takes what the
                     title and the icons leave and wraps inside it, however many
                     lines that comes to. Not justified, for the reason given in
                     the portrait file: it is a status line and not a
                     paragraph. -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/freshness"
                    android:layout_width="0dp"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/space_m"
                    android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/space_m"
                    android:layout_weight="1"
                    android:justificationMode="none"
                    android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.RoueLibre.Secondary"
                    tools:text="Mis à jour il y a 12 secondes" />

                <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                    android:id="@+id/open_map"
                    style="@style/Widget.Material3.Button.IconButton"
                    android:layout_width="@dimen/touch_target_min"
                    android:layout_height="@dimen/touch_target_min"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/stations_open_map"
                    app:icon="@drawable/ic_map_place"
                    app:iconTint="@color/ink" />

                <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                    android:id="@+id/open_favourites"
                    style="@style/Widget.Material3.Button.IconButton"
                    android:layout_width="@dimen/touch_target_min"
                    android:layout_height="@dimen/touch_target_min"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/favourites_open"
                    app:icon="@drawable/ic_favourite"
                    app:iconTint="@color/ink" />

                <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                    android:id="@+id/open_settings"
                    style="@style/Widget.Material3.Button.IconButton"
                    android:layout_width="@dimen/touch_target_min"
                    android:layout_height="@dimen/touch_target_min"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/settings_open"
                    app:icon="@drawable/ic_settings"
                    app:iconTint="@color/ink" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <!-- `flagNoExtractUi`, as in portrait: it is what refuses the
                 keyboard's own full-screen copy of this field, and this
                 arrangement would be for nothing under one. -->
            <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout
                android:id="@+id/search_field"
                style="@style/Widget.RoueLibre.SearchField"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/space_l"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_s"
                android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/space_l"
                android:hint="@string/search_stations_hint"
                app:endIconContentDescription="@string/search_stations_clear"
                app:endIconMode="clear_text">

                <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputEditText
                    android:id="@+id/search_input"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:imeOptions="actionSearch|flagNoExtractUi"
                    android:inputType="text"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.RoueLibre.Body" />
            </com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout>

            <!-- The "bikes" / "docks" toggle (SPEC §7.1), under the field: the
                 two of them are what one does to the list, and they stay
                 together. -->
            <io.github.mgdx.rouelibre.ui.ToggleRow
                android:id="@+id/mode_toggle"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/space_l"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_m"
                android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/space_l"
                app:selectionRequired="true"
                app:singleSelection="true">

                <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                    android:id="@+id/mode_bikes"
                    style="@style/Widget.RoueLibre.Toggle.Choice"
                    android:text="@string/mode_bikes" />

                <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                    android:id="@+id/mode_docks"
                    style="@style/Widget.RoueLibre.Toggle.Choice"
                    android:text="@string/mode_docks" />
            </io.github.mgdx.rouelibre.ui.ToggleRow>
        </LinearLayout>
    </androidx.core.widget.NestedScrollView>

    <!-- The rows, in the other half, from the top of the screen to the bottom
         of it. Nothing costs them height any more, so what the keyboard gives
         back is theirs.

         The room under the last row is kept, and has to be: the button floats
         over this column's bottom corner, and `StationListFragment` still
         raises both by the height of the banner when there is one. -->
    <androidx.swiperefreshlayout.widget.SwipeRefreshLayout
        android:id="@+id/swipe_refresh"
        android:layout_width="0dp"
        android:layout_height="0dp"
        app:layout_constraintBottom_toBottomOf="parent"
        app:layout_constraintEnd_toEndOf="parent"
        app:layout_constraintTop_toTopOf="parent"
        app:layout_constraintWidth_default="percent"
        app:layout_constraintWidth_percent="0.5">

        <androidx.recyclerview.widget.RecyclerView
            android:id="@+id/stations"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="match_parent"
            android:background="?attr/colorSurface"
            android:clipToPadding="false"
            android:paddingBottom="@dimen/list_room_under_the_last_row"
            android:scrollbars="vertical"
            tools:itemCount="6"
            tools:listitem="@layout/item_station" />
    </androidx.swiperefreshlayout.widget.SwipeRefreshLayout>

    <!-- An empty screen: an invitation to act, not a statement (SPEC §7). In
         the middle of the rows' column, which is the place it takes in
         portrait, that column being the whole screen there. Its side spacing
         is the ordinary one and not portrait's wide one: the column is already
         half a screen. -->
    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/empty_state"
        android:layout_width="0dp"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/space_l"
        android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/space_l"
        android:gravity="center_horizontal"
        android:orientation="vertical"
        android:visibility="gone"
        app:layout_constraintBottom_toBottomOf="@id/swipe_refresh"
        app:layout_constraintEnd_toEndOf="@id/swipe_refresh"
        app:layout_constraintStart_toStartOf="@id/swipe_refresh"
        app:layout_constraintTop_toTopOf="@id/swipe_refresh"
        tools:visibility="visible">

        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/empty_title"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:gravity="center"
            android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.RoueLibre.Title"
            tools:text="Aucune station chargée" />

        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/empty_message"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_s"
            android:gravity="center"
            android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.RoueLibre.Secondary"
            tools:text="Tire la liste vers le bas pour récupérer les stations du réseau." />

        <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
            android:id="@+id/empty_action"
            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/touch_target_min"
            android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_l"
            tools:text="Rafraîchir" />
    </LinearLayout>

    <!--
        Nearest station first (SPEC §7.2), over the bottom corner of the rows'
        column as in portrait — of the column, not of the screen, and the column
        runs the whole height of the window. That is what settles where it
        lands: hanging from a column a header had shortened to 302 px, it sat
        239 px down and bit into the first station's name; over a column that
        starts at the top of the screen it is back among the last rows, where
        the padding under the last one is what lets them be scrolled clear of
        it.

        It is still the screen's own end edge, the columns being laid out with
        the rows against it, so the thumb finds it where it found it. Last in
        the layout, so it draws over the rows; nothing is constrained to it.
    -->
    <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
        android:id="@+id/locate_me"
        style="@style/Widget.Material3.Button.IconButton.Filled"
        android:layout_width="@dimen/touch_target_min"
        android:layout_height="@dimen/touch_target_min"
        android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/space_m"
        android:layout_marginBottom="@dimen/space_m"
        android:contentDescription="@string/stations_order_by_distance"
        app:backgroundTint="@color/signal"
        app:icon="@drawable/ic_my_location"
        app:iconTint="@color/surface_on_signal"
        app:layout_constraintBottom_toBottomOf="@id/swipe_refresh"
        app:layout_constraintEnd_toEndOf="@id/swipe_refresh" />

    <!-- That the button is working, while the fix is waited for. Over the
         button and taking its foreground, for the reasons written in the
         portrait file. -->
    <com.google.android.material.progressindicator.CircularProgressIndicator
        android:id="@+id/locating"
        android:layout_width="@dimen/touch_target_min"
        android:layout_height="@dimen/touch_target_min"
        android:importantForAccessibility="no"
        android:indeterminate="true"
        android:visibility="gone"
        app:indicatorColor="@color/surface_on_signal"
        app:indicatorInset="0dp"
        app:layout_constraintBottom_toBottomOf="@id/locate_me"
        app:layout_constraintEnd_toEndOf="@id/locate_me"
        app:layout_constraintStart_toStartOf="@id/locate_me"
        app:layout_constraintTop_toTopOf="@id/locate_me"
        app:minHideDelay="500"
        app:showDelay="500"
        app:trackColor="@android:color/transparent"
        app:trackThickness="2dp"
        tools:visibility="visible" />

</androidx.constraintlayout.widget.ConstraintLayout>
